    "explanation": "A number that is a multiple of both 4 and 6 must also be a multiple of 12, their lowest common multiple. Checking each option in turn, 24 divided by 12 equals exactly 2 and 36 divided by 12 equals exactly 3, so both of those row numbers divide evenly with no remainder. Dividing 18 by 12 and dividing 30 by 12 both leave a remainder, so neither of those row numbers divides evenly. This means only 24 and 36 satisfy the stadium's compound seating rule.",
